&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Permanent position available with a considerable portfolio of works for the next 5+ years&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;To build your career by assisting in the delivery of ‘leading edge’ engineering projects.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;To work with a vibrant, agile and multi-functional team in delivering projects on time, safely, to budget and to the required quality standards.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;To benefit from Kirby’s Career Development Programmes that will enhance your leadership capability.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;To work with the best.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Excellent package on offer with room for negotiations&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Kirby Group Engineering&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Kirby Group Engineering is an international multi-disciplinary engineering services contractor and leading provider of high-value engineering services to a number of ‘blue chip’ companies. Operating across Ireland, the UK, Europe and South Africa, Kirby has become the engineering service provider of choice in growth segments such as pharmaceuticals, data centres and power transmission and distribution. Our culture is innovative, collaborative and performance focused. The successful candidate will have the opportunity to grow and develop in a company committed to developing talent and rewarding performance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role Purpose&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;The Electrical QC Inspector ensures that electrical systems, components, and installations comply with safety and quality standards. The role includes conducting inspections, testing, and documenting results to verify that work meets project requirements, codes, and industry standards.&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Functions:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Inspection of Electrical Installations:&lt;/strong&gt; Inspect electrical systems and installations during and after the construction process to ensure compliance with safety regulations, project specifications, and industry standards (e.g., NEC, IEC).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Quality Control Monitoring:&lt;/strong&gt; Monitor and verify electrical works for quality control, ensuring all installations adhere to engineering drawings, plans, and specifications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Testing and Verification:&lt;/strong&gt; Perform a variety of electrical tests (e.g., continuity tests, insulation resistance tests, voltage tests) to verify the functionality and safety of installed systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Documentation: &lt;/strong&gt;Maintain and complete detailed inspection records, non-conformance reports (NCRs), and testing logs. Provide feedback to supervisors and project managers regarding quality-related issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Non-Conformance&lt;/strong&gt; Handling: Identify and report non-conformance items, working with relevant personnel to resolve issues, ensuring corrective actions are implemented.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaborate with Site Engineers:&lt;/strong&gt; Work closely with engineers and contractors to resolve quality-related issues and ensure work is executed according to project specifications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Safety Compliance:&lt;/strong&gt; Ensure all electrical work is performed safely, adhering to workplace safety standards and relevant electrical codes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Inspection of Materials:&lt;/strong&gt; Inspect incoming electrical materials, ensuring that components meet specified standards and quality levels before being used in installations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Continuous Improvement:&lt;/strong&gt; Provide feedback and suggestions for improvements in processes, materials, and quality control systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Necessary requirement of the Quality Control Inspector:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong Trade/Construction background and/or a third level qualification in Electrical/Mechanical Engineering.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A minimum of 3 year’s experience in a lead/managerial position.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication and people skills with the ability to adapt.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work on own initiative is essential as well as taking direction where required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work in conjunction with others and be a team player.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commitment to working to the highest possible standards and delivering high quality results.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficient in the use of MS office, BIM 360 Field Management or similar platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data Centre, Pharma or similar experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Desired competencies / special roles requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in Electrical Testing &amp;amp; Commissioning&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;CompEx Ex01-04 training&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience of working on HV/MV systems. ‘Authorised person’ experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;For more information on this or opportunities based in Ireland, UK or Europe contact the&amp;nbsp;Talent Acquisition Team in Kirby Group confidentially on&amp;nbsp;+353 (0)1 454 0411 or apply in confidence.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;For more information on this role, or other Construction / Engineering opportunities across Ireland, the UK, Europe, or South Africa please review our careers page (&lt;a href=&quot;https://careers.kirbygroup.com/vacancies/&quot;&gt;Vacancies - Kirby Group Careers&lt;/a&gt;) or contact the Talent Acquisition Team at Kirby Group in confidence on +353 (0)1 454 0411.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Kirby Group Engineering is an equal opportunities employer. We are committed to fostering an inclusive workplace and welcome applications from all suitably qualified candidates, regardless of race, gender, disability, religion, sexual orientation, or age.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;You will help the Firefox DOM Core team improve the health of the Session History area. You will write tests to improve the coverage; you will fix tests and/or problems to improve the Gecko correctness.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Write Web-Platform tests to improve the coverage, and Gecko mochitests as needed&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Fix the problems and pass the tests to improve the Gecko correctness&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Work through code review with the relevant Gecko module owners and iterate to landing&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Definition of done&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Improved Session History test coverage and code correctness in Gecko, measured by passed test cases, allowing the team’s senior engineers to focus on security, performance and strategic projects.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Substantial experience in a browser-engine codebase or in automating for a browser-engine, ideally Firefox/Gecko.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Solid Javascript and applying that language skill to write automated tests.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Proficiency in and experience developing software in C++.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Strong debugging skills in a mature larget codebase.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Comfort working in the open: public bugs, code review, and upstream landing.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Prior contributions to Gecko or another major browser engine.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Familiarity with web standards and Web Platform Tests.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>
